From acc9e5706765508316a76df5a3879bcf8d5e4b59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@users.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 04:26:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] VPVulkan: VK_KHR_dynamic_rendering_local_read (in-pass
 barriers split the pass, attachments read through copies)

A vkCmdPipelineBarrier inside a render pass or dynamic rendering is recorded (OpLocalRead). When
a later draw of that pass reads one of its attachments as a texture or input attachment, the
translation stores the pass, copies each attachment read into a driver-owned texture of the same
shape (one per image, kept until the image is destroyed), reopens the pass loading its contents
and rebinds the reads to the copies. Metal cannot sample an attachment of the open encoder, and
framebuffer fetch reads colour only while Source 2's soft particles (spritecard, 136 of Alyx's
recorded pipelines) read the multiview depth/stencil attachment, so this is the exact path.
Barriers with no such read cost nothing. vkCmdSetRenderingAttachmentLocationsKHR /
InputAttachmentIndicesKHR accept the identity mapping (a remap is logged).

Test: gpu_vulkan.local_read.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P8F98JbsaD2Vbgvi6v4LyY
